    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To synthesize SSML with voice and prosody controls, I will use Amazon Polly, a text-to-speech service that turns text into lifelike speech. The code will import the necessary modules from the boto3 library, which is the AWS SDK for Python. It will then define a function to synthesize SSML, which will use the Amazon Polly client to call the synthesize_speech method with the provided SSML and voice ID. The response will be written to a local file. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789862718869,
          "start": 1789862716417
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc21a401001mRoo4Sd3Re7hzF",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc219eb6001BcjqCf7Y1XFZ3b",
      "session_id": "ses_f43de615bffevZn0bwVs573Bef",
